{"step_index":131,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-08T02:58:19Z","input_tokens":6005,"cache_read_tokens":126527,"output_tokens":3104,"thinking":"The identified path typo in the test file is the likely root cause of the `exceljs` failure. Correcting the single backslash escape in the path is crucial for enabling the library to function correctly. The correction script needs to be designed to produce two output files. The Excel output will be located at `C:\\Users\\lg\\Desktop\\Today\\(데이터검증팀)실사 DB 취합_전달용_260720_배현명_교정완료.xlsx`. A CSV output also is desired for this correction script.\n\n\nVerifying the output Excel file's structure is essential, particularly the sheet names, data ranges (excluding empty rows at the end), and the formatting of the header row. Corrected cells for `배현명` require specific styling: blue font, light blue fill, and a thin border. The summary sheet necessitates a specific, detailed table format to document all corrections, providing an easy-to-review audit trail for the team. Detailed cell-level corrections for `배현명` rows need exact implementation, specifically addressing the first identified instance of data corruption at line 5435.\n\n\nIdentified and corrected several single-column data entry errors, including incorrect values and misplaced data. Specifically, addressed issues of incorrect codes, wrong employee counts, and the merging of unrelated data within cells. These errors were found across multiple lines, and each correction has been logged.\n\n\nIdentified and corrected several typos within the 'Remark' column, specifically addressing phrases related to business status and accurate business registration numbers. Also, the business registration numbers in Column 3 were corrected according to the provided data.\n\nConfirmed the phone number format within the specified column uses hyphens; therefore, standardized mobile numbers beginning with '10' to the format '010-xxxx-xxxx'.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"const ExcelJS = require('C:/Users/lg/.gemini/antigravity/worktrees/resilient-bardeen/analyze_bae_pattern_data/node_modules/exceljs');\n\nasync function testPerformance() {\n    console.time('Workbook creation');\n    const wb = new ExcelJS.Workbook();\n    const ws = wb.addWorksheet('Test');\n\n    for (let r = 1; r <= 20504; r++) {\n        const row = [];\n        for (let c = 1; c <= 25; c++) {\n            row.push(`R${r}C${c}`);\n        }\n        const added = ws.addRow(row);\n        if (r % 500 === 0) {\n            added.getCell(2).fill = {\n                type: 'pattern',\n                pattern: 'solid',\n                fgColor: { argb: 'FFD9E1F2' }\n            };\n            added.getCell(2).font = { color: { argb: 'FF002060' }, bold: true };\n        }\n    }\n    console.timeEnd('Workbook creation');\n\n    console.time('Write to buffer/file');\n    // Just test in memory\n    const buffer = await wb.xlsx.writeBuffer();\n    console.timeEnd('Write to buffer/file');\n    console.log('Buffer size MB:', (buffer.length / (1024 * 1024)).toFixed(2));\n}\n\ntestPerformance().catch(console.error);\n","Description":"Benchmark ExcelJS performance with 20504 rows","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\f5c8b43a-5c52-40dc-83ac-10d0b6555d1e\\scratch\\benchmark_excel.js","toolAction":"Benchmarking ExcelJS","toolSummary":"Benchmark ExcelJS"}}]}
